  "query_preview": "..\n/Issued 105 PM MDT Mon Sep 14 2026/ \n\n - Meteorological Overview: \n\nAs the upper-level low continues its easterly track out of the \nregion, it will be followed by a weaker upper-level ridge. This \nridge will bring a period of milder winds and overall drier \nconditions Monday night through Wednesday night, although areas \nof showers can't be ruled out. As a weaker upper-level low moves \neasterly into the region Thursday afternoon/evening, it is \nexpected to bring widespread shower and thunderstorm potential. \nThe low will continue to track easterly through the region over \nFriday and Saturday, which will allow for the potential of showers\nand thunderstorms to continue. An upper-level ridge will follow \nthis upper-level low, bringing warm, dry, and milder weather on \nSunday and Monday. -ESH\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios: \n\nMain concern will be strong wind gusts over 55 mph today. Fergus \ncounty continues to have the highest potential (areas of 70%< \nchance of 24 hr max wind gusts at or above 55 mph), so it \ncontinues to have a High Wind Warning until 6 pm MDT. \n\nFor the shower event beginning Thursday afternoon/evening and \ncontinuing through Saturday, highest totals are expected in the \nsouthern half of the region (around 50% chance of rain totals .25\"\nor above between Thursday 6 AM- Saturday 6 AM MDT). \n\nCurrent time period for highest thunderstorm probability is 12 pm\nFriday-12 am Saturday MDT, 20-35% chance across the region. -ESH",
